TIP:  The (A6) is just (A) with the 1st string covered.  I prefer to play it like an (A) with my middle three fingers and use my pinky to cover to 1st string but you can play it as a four-string barre as well.  Whatever is most comfortable. 

TIP:  The (Bm) follows (D) so you can just add your pinky to the 3rd string/4th fret if you don’t want to come off the (D) to reposition for a fuller (Bm). 
   
  
